                    "What changed is one decision applied three ways, and it is datable.  He stopped making videos about objects and started making videos about principles.  The old block is a specific radio or receiver, restored across more than one upload: a Hammarlund SP-600 split over 13 and 21 March, a 1961 DeWald FM receiver at 52 minutes on 26 April.  The new block is a question with an answer demonstrated on the bench, and the titles are locked into that grammar: Why Twist Wire, Why Add A Capacitor Across The Switch, Why Connect A Resistor And Capacitor Across Relay Contacts.  He test-fired the format on <mark>11 February</mark> with a tantalum capacitor video that did 118,375 at a time when his uploads were mostly running in the tens of thousands, sat on it, then proved it at scale on <mark>7 June</mark> with an audio cable video at 522,428.  From there it is the default.  Runtime followed: the restoration era ran 27 to 52 minutes, the new format sits at <mark>9 to 19 minutes</mark>, and he has stopped splitting a repair across uploads at all.",
