                    "Boots launched For Gifts They'll Really Love on Wednesday, a <mark>60-second</mark> film and the first Christmas work under its Give it Some Boots platform.  Directed by Phoebe Arnstein of Biscuit Filmworks, who also did the September platform launch films.  The idea is a single structure repeated: Christmas morning, then jumps forward through the year showing the gifts in daily use, a mother in a light-therapy mask taking the bins out, a woman reaching for a hair styler mid dinner date.  Set to a reworking of Shepherd of the Bells.",
                    "The part worth stealing is the edit list, and it is unusually explicit.  Off that one film Boots is running its <mark>first 20-second television edits plus 18 offer-led edits</mark> carrying Star Gifts and its three-for-two promotion across more than 1,200 products.  Plus the brand's <mark>first Netflix takeover</mark>, across launch and Black Friday.  A multi-channel television roadblock on <mark>6 November</mark>, Snapchat, TikTok Top Search, curated Reddit gift guides, a special build at Westfield White City and taxi wraps, then Underground and rail in the new year.  And it says it will use <mark>real-time footfall data</mark> to steer digital spend towards driving shop visits during the campaign.",
