                    "So why run it.  Because the mechanism is a scheduling decision rather than a creative one, and it is the cheapest multiplier in brand video.  Eighteen cutdowns off one shoot cost almost nothing if the edit list existed before the camera rolled, and cost two or three times as much if it arrives afterwards, because you are then conforming a finished grade, re-clearing music for new durations and discovering that nothing holds long enough to put a price card over it.  The footfall part is the same discipline one level up: deciding in advance which number will redirect the money, so that the redirection is a rule rather than an argument in week three.",
